\title{Low-Degree Testing, from FRI to WHIR}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    The heart of the transparent stack. The lineage is short and each step answers one specific
    complaint: [FRI](dhsorens-0037) tests proximity to a Reed–Solomon code by folding,
    [STIR](dhsorens-003B) attacks its query cost at constant rate, and [WHIR](dhsorens-003C) attacks
    STIR's verification cost while joining the univariate and multilinear worlds.
}

\p{
    These pages should be the most careful in the corpus. The soundness statements are where the
    [regimes](dhsorens-0038) matter, where the deployed parameters are conjectural, and where
    [ArkLib](dhsorens-0040)'s hardest formalisation work sits.
}

